1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,140
Listen to a talk in a neuroscience class.

2
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:02,722
Man:

3
00:00:02,722 --> 00:00:05,611
Today we’re exploring neuroplasticity,

4
00:00:05,611 --> 00:00:11,270
which means the brain’s ability to reorganize itself by forming new neural connections throughout life.

5
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:19,260
Neuroplasticity allows the brain to adapt in response to learning, experience, and other stimulation.

6
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:27,150
This remarkable capacity for change is crucial for cognitive development and skill acquisition.

7
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:33,240
There are two main types of neuroplasticity: structural and functional.

8
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:42,944
Structural neuroplasticity involves changes in the physical structure of the brain, such as the growth of new neurons

9
00:00:42,944 --> 00:00:45,150
or the strengthening of synapses.

10
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:53,193
Functional neuroplasticity, on the other hand, refers to changes in the brain’s activity patterns,

11
00:00:53,193 --> 00:00:59,050
allowing different areas to take over functions previously managed by underperforming regions.

12
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:06,087
For example, if a region responsible for language processing becomes less active, nearby

13
00:01:06,087 --> 00:01:11,240
or even distant areas may increase their activity to support language functions.

14
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:18,894
Now, research has shown that engaging in activities that stimulate the brain, such as

15
00:01:18,894 --> 00:01:21,619
learning new skills, physical exercise,

16
00:01:21,619 --> 00:01:27,290
and cognitive training, can enhance both structural and functional neuroplasticity.

17
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:36,233
Consider aerobic exercises like running or swimming—they help the brain by boosting a special

18
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:38,098
protein called BDNF,

19
00:01:38,098 --> 00:01:43,010
which works like fertilizer for brain cells, helping them grow and stay healthy.

20
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:51,180
Understanding neuroplasticity has important implications for creating strategies that promote brain resilience.

21
00:01:51,180 --> 00:02:02,120
By leveraging neuroplasticity, researchers and practitioners aim to support cognitive vitality in people of all ages.
